\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. ALL as God wills, who wisely heeds
\par To give or withold,
\par And knoweth more of all my needs 
\par Than all my prayers have told.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Enough that blessings undeserved
\par Have marked my erring track;
\par That wheresoe'er my sweet have swerved,
\par His chastening turned me back;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. That more and more a providence
\par Of love is understood,
\par Making the springs of time and sense
\par Sweet with eternal good;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. That death seems but a covered way
\par Which opens into light
\par Wherein no blinded child can stray
\par Beyond the Father's sight;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. That care and trial seem at last,
\par Through memory's sunset air,
\par Like mountains ranges overpast,
\par In purple distance fair;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. That all the jarring notes of life
\par Seem blending in a psalm,
\par And all the angels of its strife
\par Slow rounding into calm.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. And so the shadows fall apart,
\par And so the west winds play;
\par And all the windows of my heart
\par I open to the day.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

